# Nylux Dawnshield, Venerable Martyr of the 32nd Choir
Nylux was born an orphaned half-elf and raised in one of the many Church-controlled orphanages of the True Revelations. Like countless other children, he was conscripted young. He began as a medic, patching the wounded between battles, then trained as a full soldier and thrown into the meat grinder as expendable fodder.

He survived. More than that, he thrived. Through years of campaigning against the hordes of darkness he earned a distinguished record, marked by absolute loyalty and a zealotry that never wavered, even when the last of his mortal life drained away on some forgotten battlefield.

The Church did not let him rest. His corpse was recovered at once. All flesh was stripped from the bones. The skeleton was etched with gilded arcane glyphs and holy symbols, then a blessed crystal was sealed inside the skull. The crystal fused his lingering spirit to the enhanced bones and bound him to the essence of an Angelic Celestial allied with the Church. In that moment he ceased to be a man and became one of the sanctified dead: a Venerable Martyr.

For centuries afterward he served the 32nd Choir as an instrument of holy war. Unstoppable faith and relentless purpose made him a terror to the forces of darkness. They feared him enough to risk a great deal to be rid of him. In the end they succeeded in banishing him from the world entirely, severing both his power and the link that had once joined him to the Angel who shared his soul.

Cast adrift across the multiverse, Nylux now wanders. He still seeks darkness to battle, following the faintest remaining threads of the divine in the hope of one day restoring the bond with the Angel that once burned within him.

# Venerable Martyr / Sanctified Dead
(Custom Background – Healer Origin Feat)

The Church of True Revelations does not waste the faithful. When a soldier of proven zeal falls in battle against the hordes of darkness, the body is reclaimed if it can be reached. Flesh is carefully stripped away. The clean bones are engraved with precise gilded arcane glyphs and sacred symbols that reinforce the skeleton and anchor residual spirit. A single blessed crystal is then set into the skull. Through a rite known only to the highest ranks of the Church, the crystal fuses the lingering soul to the enhanced bones and simultaneously binds that soul to a fragment of an Angelic Celestial allied with the Church.

The result is a Sanctified Dead, more specifically a Venerable Martyr when the individual has already demonstrated exceptional loyalty and service in life. These beings are neither mindless undead nor free-willed revenants. They retain their memories, personality, and sense of purpose, yet their existence is now sustained by holy power rather than flesh or blood. Pain is distant. Exhaustion is optional. Fear of death is largely irrelevant. What remains is duty, sharpened to a pure and relentless edge.

## Lailahriela, The Iron Rapture
She is a powerful Angelic celestial entity who embodies the raw vitality of existence through what she calls the Three F’s: Feasting, Fighting, and Fornicating. To her these are not separate pursuits but three expressions of the same holy drive—to fully inhabit the body, the moment, and the world with unrestrained appetite.

Her concept breaks down into three core pillars:
* **Feast**: She has an almost foodie-like love of new dishes, drinks, and experiences. She will send her champion to cross borders, topple obstacles, or open new lands simply to taste what has never been tasted before. Shared meals, victory feasts, and the discovery of unfamiliar flavors are as holy to her as any battlefield.
* **Fight**: She revels in the clash of arms, the surge of adrenaline, and the protection of her chosen. Combat is a feast of its own; every shield raised and every enemy broken is an act of vigorous, living devotion.
* **Fornicate**: She honors the body’s capacity for passion and closeness. Desire is treated as a natural, sacred hunger rather than something hidden or shameful.

She is most commonly encountered as a seventeen-foot-tall, mirror-armored angel of passionate preservation and vigorous conquest, possessing four midnight-indigo wings tipped in blinding starlight. Her theme is the meeting of night and day: golden celestial energy highlighted by silvery strands of moonlight and wisps of pearlescent starlight. This light can knit wounds with a rush of warmth and endorphins or burn away threats that endanger her champion.

In short, she is a force of appetite—hungry for battle, for connection, and for the next new taste—once bound to Nylux as both guardian and the living embodiment of everything he once fought to protect and seeks to reclaim.
